  "sourceState": "Revision 3 preserves the complete caller-backed Forms state boundary and implements pinned gaps rather than copying defects: atomic first-revision creation, cancellation-safe and idempotently retryable admitted-revision register-and-publish, one-current-published listing, immutable tenant-scoped lifecycle and lineage, lossless Carrier authoring metadata, bounded CP-locked reuse-by-reference, one atomic tenant/Party/actor scope, form-bound draft resume/abandon, and ephemeral pre-auth promote-or-purge. Eight source-derived suites plus nine gap cases pass 130 native tests. Clean npm/NuGet consumers prove wire and state behavior with no source/project fallback or assembly ambiguity. Durable aggregate adapters and executable render/validate/submit, audit, outbox, and recovery remain assigned to the complete Forms Engine gate.",
